  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Tested with default emotes and custom emotes.\nWhen you trigger emotes in SDK3 avatars through the radial menu, the Head IK does not disable at the same time the animation is played, causing the head to look forward for a second before snapping to where it should be facing in the animation. This does not happen in SDK2 avatars.\nImage 1: examples of the snapping with an avatar from the 3.0 hub world, using default emotes\nImage 2: close up example of the snapping with a custom avatar with a custom emote that spins the body around\nImage 3: the same avatar/animation as image 2, but in Live instead of the beta\nAdditionally, the avatar gets pushed forward when using an emote, get pushed backwards while the emote happens, and then pushed forwards again after the emote ends\nImage 4 and 5 are comparisons of how it is in the Beta vs Live respectively, although with different animations (image 5 however is also undesirable because emotes cause the body to block the head in live)",
